@{ ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy & data"; }
<div class="page-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Your learning, your data</p><h1>Privacy &amp; data</h1></div></div>
<div class="panel">
    <h2>Account and activity</h2><p>Your account, submitted code, test results and saved AI advice are stored to support your learning history. Your submission details and progress are available to your signed-in account. The public leaderboard displays your display name and learning statistics; it does not display your email.</p>
    <h2>AI feedback is your choice</h2><p>Clicking Analyze with AI sends your code, the task description, compiler diagnostics where relevant, and visible failed-test details to OpenAI. Hidden test contents and account credentials are excluded. Requests disable stored Responses output; OpenAI's applicable service data policies still apply. Advice is saved with your submission and reused for later views.</p>
    <h2>Local browser storage</h2><p>A sign-in cookie keeps you authenticated. Security cookies protect form submissions. The editor keeps a draft for each task in this browser tab's session storage; drafts are not shared with other accounts.</p>
    <h2>Using a shared device</h2><p>Log out and close the browser tab when you finish. Contact the platform administrator about account or data questions.</p>
</div>
